# g96-be-tools-b: what the lead applies after the wave

## mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs (hot)
Two edits in the same function (the one that builds `project_registry`, the `Catalog` over `b.core_state`).

1. Anchor: the `code_graph` tool's `UserTrustedRoots` literal, where the registry Arc is moved today:
       registry: project_registry,
   becomes
       registry: project_registry.clone(),
   (without it the Arc is moved before the worktree chain below and edit 2 does not compile).

2. Anchor: the `Worktrees::new(...)` chain, directly after the line
       .with_root_cleanup(Arc::new(crate::worktree_cache_cleanups::CodeGraphCleanup::new(code_graph_cache.clone(), b.tokens.maintenance_io)))
   add the line
       .with_root_cleanup(Arc::new(crate::worktree_cache_cleanups::TrustedRootCleanup::new(project_registry.clone())))

This is `forgetTrustedCodeGraphRoot`: a removed worktree root also leaves the project registry. No Cargo change
(mixdog-workspace and mixdog-scm are already dependencies of mixdog-app-server-daemon).

## Callers of the new counts
ExecRuntime::other_owner_shell_work(&ThreadId) -> (foreground, background) in mixdog-tools exec/jobs.rs is the Rust
`otherSessionBackgroundShellJobCount`; its caller is the task list (exec/task.rs). The Node caller
session-runtime/workspace/transitions.mjs (defaultOwnShellJobCount) already has its Rust twin: WorktreeHost::shell_job_count
(mixdog-app-server-daemon host_runtime_draft.rs, read by mixdog-core-session worktree_merge.rs); nothing to wire for it.
SERVICE_PENDING: no names to remove.
